# interplay_limits_root_range_full: In the blocks setup the root task's range allocator (0xffffff bytes in 16 KiB granules) maps the root node, the root FIFO, each local task's root page, each child's page list for a moment and its ring, each display's shared page and each device info page. Filled exactly, 1024 pages, by the root node, the largest root FIFO (8 pages), all 256 tasks (256 root pages) and children 1-59 (rings of 13 pages, every entry of a page list naming one page, and child 59's of 5): children 60-63 cannot be placed, still signal their define and never run (-start's result is ignored). With nothing left, a display connect (opcode 1) and GetDeviceInfo (58) are tried on port 0: both fault. Deleting tasks 200-255 frees 56 pages: a connect on port 1 and the device info work, and a child that never ran, deleted and defined again, runs. In the map and isolate setups nothing is allocated from that range (under isolation only task 0 is local), and every child runs, and the connect on port 0 and the device info work at once.
